.TH RAILCAR 1 "November 2026" "Railcar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
railcar \- terminal client for the Tieroute chat protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B railcar
[\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-log\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-dev\-server\fR \fINAME\fR=\fIURL\fR]...
.br
.B railcar \-\-demo
.br
.B railcar \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Railcar is a terminal client for Tieroute, a federated, end-to-end encrypted
(E2EE) chat protocol, from Reroute Holdings LLC. It has direct chats, group
chats, communities, files, profiles, presence, read receipts, backups, moves
to another homeserver, reports, calls, and voice channels.
.PP
The first time it runs, Railcar asks for a homeserver, a handle, and the
homeserver's registration code, or signs in with another device or the
recovery code. Type \fB?\fR for every key, and \fB:\fR or Ctrl+P for the
command palette.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " DIR"
Keep the identity, keys, and messages in \fIDIR\fR. The default is
\fI~/.config/railcar\fR on Linux, or the system's configuration folder.
.TP
.B \-\-key\-file
When there's no system keychain, keep the profile's key in a file in the
profile directory. Anyone who can read the directory can then read your keys
and messages.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Write debug lines to \fIFILE\fR. They hold request paths and errors, never
message text or keys.
.TP
.BI \-\-dev\-server " NAME=URL"
Reach the server \fINAME\fR at \fIURL\fR, for local test networks. Give it
once for each server.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Run with made-up chats and no network, to try the interface.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help.
.SH CALLS
In a direct chat or a group chat, \fB:call\fR rings the others. A ring rings
the terminal bell and shows a notification; \fB:answer\fR and
\fB:decline\-call\fR answer it. In a call, \fB:mute\fR, \fB:unmute\fR,
\fB:deafen\fR, and \fB:hangup\fR. In a community's voice channel,
\fB:join\-voice\fR and \fB:leave\-voice\fR. A bar above the status bar shows
the call, how long it has lasted, who's in it, who's muted, and who's
speaking.
.PP
Calls use the default microphone and speakers. They're relayed through your
homeserver's TURN relay, so nobody learns your IP address.
\fB:direct\-calls on\fR lets them connect directly, which shows your IP
address to the people you call and to community servers.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/railcar
The default profile: the identity, its keys, and its messages, encrypted
with a key kept in the system keychain.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Tieroute specification, at https://rerouteholdings.llc/specs/tieroute.
.SH AUTHOR
Reroute Holdings LLC.
